One file per Plan2001 target (ISA): amd64 (supported), arm64 (planned,
phase 4), riscv64 (future).  Every tool takes TARGET (default amd64) and
reads tools/targets/$TARGET; a target whose status is not "supported"
is refused with a clear message.  The syntax is the common part of bash
and rc: name=value, name=(list), # comments - so the file can be
sourced by bash and by rc in the build VM (tools/build.rc).
The syntax also permits parsing by host-side tools. bootarch is BootInfo.arch
(sys/include/bootinfo.h).
